# Cursor Rules for Employee HR Mobile Application

## 🎯 Project Overview
This is a mobile-first, progressive web app (PWA) built with Svelte + Inertia.js + Laravel. The application follows modern mobile app design patterns and emphasizes code quality, performance, and maintainability.

## 🏗️ Architecture & Technology Stack

### Frontend (Svelte + Inertia.js)
- **Framework**: Svelte 5+ with TypeScript
- **Routing**: Inertia.js for seamless SPA-like navigation
- **State Management**: Use Svelte stores and reactive statements
- **UI Components**: Use the existing UI component library in `resources/js/components/ui/`
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with mobile-first responsive design

### Backend (Laravel)
- **PHP Version**: 8.1+
- **Authentication**: Employee-specific guard with session management
- **API Design**: RESTful endpoints with proper validation
- **Database**: Eloquent ORM with proper relationships
- **Security**: CSRF protection, rate limiting, input validation

## 📱 Mobile-First Development Rules

### Responsive Design
- **Breakpoints**: Mobile (<768px), Tablet (768px-1024px), Desktop (>1024px)
- **Layout**: Mobile gets bottom navigation, desktop gets top navigation only
- **Touch Targets**: Minimum 44px × 44px for interactive elements
- **Viewport**: Always use responsive viewport meta tags

### Component Structure
```svelte
<!-- Always structure components with mobile-first approach -->
<script lang="ts">
  // TypeScript interfaces first
  // Reactive statements
  // Event handlers
  // Lifecycle methods
</script>

<!-- Mobile-first markup -->
<div class="w-full md:w-auto">
  <!-- Mobile layout -->
  <div class="block md:hidden">
    <!-- Mobile-specific content -->
  </div>

  <!-- Desktop layout -->
  <div class="hidden md:block">
    <!-- Desktop-specific content -->
  </div>
</div>
```

## 🔐 Authentication & Security Rules

### Frontend Security
- **Route Protection**: Always check authentication state before rendering protected content
- **Input Validation**: Client-side validation for immediate feedback
- **Error Handling**: Graceful error messages without exposing sensitive information
- **Session Management**: Proper logout and session cleanup

### Backend Security
- **Guard Usage**: Use `auth:employee` middleware for employee routes
- **Input Sanitization**: Always sanitize and validate user inputs
- **SQL Injection**: Use Eloquent ORM, never raw SQL queries
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement rate limiting for authentication endpoints

## 📍 Location Services Rules

### GPS Integration
- **Permission Handling**: Always request location permission gracefully
- **Fallback Strategy**: Provide alternative input methods when GPS unavailable
- **Accuracy**: Use high accuracy mode for location capture
- **Radius Validation**: Implement 100m office boundary checking

### Location Code Example
```typescript
// Always handle location errors gracefully
function getCurrentLocation(): Promise<GeolocationPosition> {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    if (!navigator.geolocation) {
      reject(new Error('Geolocation not supported'));
      return;
    }

    navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(
      resolve,
      (error) => {
        // Provide user-friendly error messages
        const errorMessages = {
          [error.PERMISSION_DENIED]: 'Location access denied. Please enable location services.',
          [error.POSITION_UNAVAILABLE]: 'Location information unavailable.',
          [error.TIMEOUT]: 'Location request timed out.'
        };
        reject(new Error(errorMessages[error.code] || 'Unknown location error'));
      },
      {
        enableHighAccuracy: true,
        timeout: 10000,
        maximumAge: 60000
      }
    );
  });
}
```

## 🎨 UI/UX Development Rules

### Component Design
- **Consistency**: Use existing UI component library consistently
- **Accessibility**: Include proper ARIA labels and semantic HTML
- **Loading States**: Always show loading indicators for async operations
- **Error States**: Provide clear error messages and recovery options

### Mobile Patterns
- **Bottom Navigation**: Use for primary navigation on mobile
- **Top Navigation**: Use for page titles and user actions
- **Cards**: Use card-based layouts for content organization
- **Touch Feedback**: Provide visual feedback for touch interactions

## 📊 State Management Rules

### Svelte Stores
- **Reactive Statements**: Use `$:` for derived state
- **Store Updates**: Use proper store update methods
- **Component State**: Keep component state local when possible
- **Global State**: Use stores for application-wide state

### Data Flow
```typescript
// Always define proper interfaces
interface Employee {
  id: number;
  first_name: string;
  last_name: string;
  email: string;
  department_id: number;
  position_id: number;
  // ... other properties
}

// Use reactive statements for derived state
$: fullName = `${employee.first_name} ${employee.last_name}`;
$: canSubmitAttendance = currentLocation && isWithinOfficeRadius();
```

## 🔧 Performance Rules

### Frontend Performance
- **Lazy Loading**: Implement lazy loading for non-critical components
- **Image Optimization**: Use appropriate image formats and sizes
- **Bundle Size**: Keep component imports minimal
- **Caching**: Implement proper caching strategies

### Backend Performance
- **Database Queries**: Use eager loading to avoid N+1 queries
- **Caching**: Implement Redis caching for frequently accessed data
- **API Response**: Keep API responses lean and focused
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement appropriate rate limiting

## 🧪 Testing Rules

### Code Quality
- **TypeScript**: Always use strict TypeScript mode
- **Error Handling**: Handle all possible error cases
- **Edge Cases**: Consider edge cases in user interactions
- **Validation**: Validate all user inputs

### Testing Strategy
- **Unit Tests**: Write tests for utility functions and components
- **Integration Tests**: Test API endpoints and component interactions
- **User Testing**: Test on actual mobile devices
- **Cross-Browser**: Test on multiple browsers and devices

## 📁 File Organization Rules

### Frontend Structure
```
resources/js/
├── components/
│   ├── ui/           # Reusable UI components
│   └── employee/     # Employee-specific components
├── layouts/
│   └── employee/     # Employee layout components
├── pages/
│   ├── auth/         # Authentication pages
│   └── employee/     # Employee feature pages
├── hooks/            # Custom Svelte hooks
├── stores/           # Svelte stores
└── types/            # TypeScript type definitions
```

### Backend Structure
```
app/
├── Http/
│   ├── Controllers/
│   │   └── Auth/     # Authentication controllers
│   ├── Middleware/    # Custom middleware
│   └── Requests/      # Form request validation
├── Models/            # Eloquent models
├── Services/          # Business logic services
└── Providers/         # Service providers
```

## 🚀 Development Workflow Rules

### Code Standards
- **Formatting**: Use Prettier for consistent code formatting
- **Linting**: Use ESLint with TypeScript rules
- **Commits**: Use conventional commit messages
- **Branches**: Use feature branches for new development

### Git Commit Convention
```
feat: add employee attendance submission
fix: resolve GPS location accuracy issue
docs: update API documentation
style: improve mobile navigation layout
refactor: simplify authentication logic
test: add attendance validation tests
```

